{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>To stand to minister.</b> Scripture teaches you that ministering is only done while standing. And it mentioned the Name of YHWH, which is the attribute of judgment, in the manner of (Exodus 20): ״אזכיר את שמי״, (Deuteronomy 12): ״לשכן שמו שם״, and so is the view of Onkelos in every place where the Holy One, blessed be He, is mentioned as 'My Name' or 'His Name' — that he translates it with the language of the Shekhinah. And from here the High Priest relied when he would mention on the Day of Atonements the Name of 42 letters, for that day is mercy within judgment, and so too is the Name; and understand this, for the seventh of the Names indicating judgment I have already mentioned at the beginning of parashat Aḥarei Mot by way of allusion, and from there you will understand it. And you will find in this parashah a number of words equal to the word-count of the blessing Magen Avraham."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:10.271558950Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}